  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/79-1.PNG\" style=\"width: 233px; height: 175px;\" /></p><p>In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;dipole moment of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is added to the&nbsp;resultant dipole moment of three <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math> bonds, hence compound&nbsp;has non-zero value of dipole moment.</p><p>Electronegativity of carbon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Electronegativity of hydrogen<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/79-2.PNG\" style=\"width: 223px; height: 189px;\" /><br />Elelctrongegativity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Electronegativity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/79-3.PNG\" style=\"width: 227px; height: 188px;\" /></p><p>Due to symmetry and similar bonds, vector summation of net&nbsp;dipole moments of both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are zero, hence equal.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
